# Line endings are a live hazard on this project, not a style question.
#
# The working tree grew up on Windows and ended up MIXED: most files CRLF, but
# js/factions.js and js/towers2.js LF. Patch scripts here read a file, edit it,
# and write it back, and one that reads with universal newlines and writes with
# newline='' silently flattens a whole 200KB file — which produces a diff that
# touches every line and hides the three that mattered. That has happened.
#
# So: the repository stores LF, and every checkout gets LF on every platform.
# One convention, no conversion layer, nothing for a patch script to guess at.
# Editors handle LF fine on Windows; git's autocrlf setting is bypassed by the
# explicit eol below, so a contributor cannot half-configure their way into the
# old mixed state.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Never touch these — a "newline fix" inside a webp is corruption.
*.webp   binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.mp3    binary
*.ogg    binary
*.wav    binary

# js/artpack.js is generated: ~4.8MB of base64 data URIs on a handful of lines.
# Diffing it is meaningless and slow, so mark it so review tools collapse it.
# It is still TEXT (the game loads it as a script) — this only affects display.
js/artpack.js linguist-generated=true -diff

# The built single-file bundles are outputs, not sources. Collapse them too.
aegis-protocol.html linguist-generated=true -diff
docs/archive/*.html linguist-generated=true -diff
